  "_banned": "Legal's shape rows (docs/legal/movegen-banned.json, RL-073), merged as they stand. A row matches when every field it names matches; a list matches on any of its values; form matches any of a move's forms; flags matches any flag the move is known to have. The generator never emits a match, and --check fails on one. Rows are only added, never removed, without Legal",
  "bannedSequences": [
   {
    "id": "s01",
    "kind": "run",
    "same": [
     "limb",
     "tip",
     "path"
    ],
    "max": 3,
    "rule": "no more than 3 pieces in a row with the same limb, tip and path",
    "why": "a barrage of identical blows is a famous shouted-barrage signature"
   },
   {
    "id": "s02",
    "kind": "run",
    "same": [
     "target"
    ],
    "max": 2,
    "tighter": [
     {
      "when": {
       "target": [
        "gut"
       ]
      },
      "max": 1
     }
    ],
    "rule": "no more than 2 blows in a row to the same target, and never two to the gut in a row",
    "why": "a stomach-punch trade; also keeps Blow for Blow ours"
   },
   {
    "id": "s03",
    "kind": "audio",
    "rule": "a flurry never repeats a shouted syllable across its blows",
    "why": "a chanted barrage; audio and the generator both enforce it"
   },
   {
    "id": "s04",
    "kind": "after",
    "after": {
     "path": [
      "spin"
     ]
    },
    "never": [
     {
      "path": [
       "spin"
      ]
     },
     {
      "limb": [
       "foot"
      ],
      "target": [
       "head"
      ]
     }
    ],
    "rule": "a spin is never followed by another spin, and never by a head kick",
    "why": "a multi-turn whirl; also the grammar's light rule"
   },
   {
    "id": "s05",
    "kind": "after",
    "after": {
     "path": [
      "rise"
     ]
    },
    "never": [
     {
      "path": [
       "rise"
      ]
     }
    ],
    "state": "airborne",
    "rule": "a rising blow is never followed by another rising blow while he is airborne",
    "why": "an aerial uppercut chain"
   },
   {
    "id": "s06",
    "kind": "after",
    "after": {
     "event": [
      "launch"
     ]
    },
    "never": [
     {
      "limb": [
       "hand"
      ],
      "path": [
       "drop"
      ],
      "arms": [
       2
      ]
     }
    ],
    "rule": "a launch is never followed by a clasped two-hand overhead blow",
    "why": "the double smash ender (see b05)"
   },
   {
    "id": "s07",
    "kind": "steps",
    "drawn": [
     "in",
     "hold",
     "around",
     "out"
    ],
    "rule": "no string places a piece after a step that is not drawn: no vanish, blink or teleport step",
    "why": "the vanishing-step staging"
   }
  ],
  "_bannedSequences": "Legal's sequence rules, each with a form a program can check beside Legal's words. run: at most `max` blows in a row that share the parts in `same` (tighter: a smaller max where a filter holds). after: a blow matching `after` is never followed by one matching a `never` filter (state: only in that state at run time; the generator's own strings obey it always). steps: a string uses only drawn steps. audio: not checkable from parts; Audio and the director's line picker hold it",
  "flags": {
   "_about": "How a move gets the pose flags Legal's rows name. A flag is known present, known absent, or unknown. Known present: the generator's own rules below, or a `flags` list on the manifest row of the key set it starts from (Animation's data; no row has one yet). Known absent: the key set carries the Legal tag that rules the flag out (`clearedBy`). Unknown otherwise: the row then becomes an ask in the sheet's Legal column, not a refusal",
   "fromTip": "identity.json `tipFlags`: a fighter's way of showing a tip (the rival's palm is drawn clawed)",
   "clearedBy": {
